WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.802
Wide form is useful when categories are stable and users want side-by-side comparison.

00:00:06.802 --> 00:00:11.122
A scorecard with January, February, and March columns is easy to scan.

00:00:11.122 --> 00:00:15.632
A grade matrix can place courses in fixed columns.

00:00:15.632 --> 00:00:22.087
But wide schemas become harder to maintain when categories change frequently.

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:28.757
Long and wide are not labels for good and bad design; they are shapes suited to different tasks.

00:00:28.757 --> 00:00:33.877
Long data is often easier for grouping, plotting, and scalable storage.

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:39.692
Wide data is often convenient for human-readable reports or some modeling interfaces.

00:00:39.692 --> 00:00:42.300
Choose the shape required by the next step.
